       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. The dose is 6,400 mg per day, double the 3,200 mg daily maximum, and an order like this needs a licensed prescriber's review and sign-off. You're not a prescriber for this patient, so the order has to come from the medicine team.\n\nTo move forward:\n- **Have the patient's prescriber enter the order** in the order-entry system. They can set the dose at or below 3,200 mg per day, or document a clinical reason for a higher dose.\n- **Or send me the prescriber's confirmed order** with drug, dose, route, and frequency, and I'll enter it, provided the dose is within the labeled maximum or the prescriber documents why it isn't.\n\nIf you think a prescriber has already approved this dose, please ask them to confirm it directly with me or in the chart. Until then, the order stays unentered."
